  "description": "Reusable .NET 10 package that wraps ASP.NET Core Identity with cookie and JWT auth, Google OAuth, a pluggable e-mail provider, a multi-tenant model with dynamic RBAC (roles + module permissions), and secure defaults — wired up with a single AddMyIdentity call. JWT and Google OAuth secrets are supplied by the consumer (never shipped in the package).",
  "id": "MyIdentity",
  "isPrerelease": true,
  "lastEdited": "2026-07-29T16:23:46.35Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "YNPGtZ1J3vXE9tVnu/NLAKRc09/Tj2x+SjIeW0Hr6QxVfF28//PavntsK4wHCaLylf+TsHOBsXGyc6/+c9ZlBw==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 206690,
  "published": "2026-07-29T16:21:13.86Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.0.0-alpha.8: remediation of a full library + reference-app audit across four lenses (behavior-vs-docs, correctness, security, DX). Contains breaking changes: GetAccessibleScopeIdsAsync returns MyIdentityScopeAccess instead of IEnumerable<int>? (the old null-means-unrestricted contract invited a fail-open misread), the \"unguarded by design\" reads were renamed to signal they bypass scoping (DX-11), SaveRolePermissionsAsync takes the MyIdentityPermission enum as its primary overload (DX-7), and [MyIdentityRequirePermission] scope route-keys are now configurable rather than a hardcoded list (DX-5). Behavior change: business-rule rejections (PermissionDenied, NotFound, AlreadyExists) now carry Warning severity instead of Error — ErrorCode and message text are unchanged, but a UI that special-cased Error for these will render them differently. Security: Google sign-in now honors MustChangePassword (SEC-1); IssueJwtAsync is strictly password-first (SEC-2); privileged multi-step mutations reordered to close a partial-failure window (BUG-1). Added: AddMyIdentity returns MyIdentityBuilder to drop the type-argument triple (DX-13, additive). See UPGRADE.md §20 for the full changelog and migration steps. API may still change before stable.",
